            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Generally no — not without removing the paint first. Epoxy applied over existing paint will bond to the paint, not the concrete. When the paint eventually fails (and it will), it takes your new epoxy with it. To apply epoxy over a painted floor, you must either grind or chemically strip the existing paint completely, confirm all traces are removed, then prep and coat the bare concrete. Some specialty adhesion-promoter primers claim to work over paint, but professional installers don't use them for a reason.",
